/*
# Demo Seed Data

Populates the schema created in the previous migration with a realistic
starter dataset for "Green Valley Apartments" so the app is immediately
usable/demoable instead of showing empty screens everywhere:
  - 1 society_settings row
  - 60 units across 3 wings (A/B/C, 20 each)
  - 5 bookable amenities
  - 5 notices
  - Bills + payments for the last 2 completed months (this month is left
    unbilled on purpose, so "Generate Bills" has something real to do)
  - Sample expenses, visitors, complaints, one resolved SOS alert, and
    amenity bookings

All names are synthetic placeholder data, matching the existing fictional
"Green Valley Apartments" already hardcoded in the app.

This migration is idempotent: everything is wrapped in a check that only
runs if the `units` table is currently empty, so it is safe even if this
migration file gets applied more than once.
*/

DO $$
BEGIN
  IF (SELECT COUNT(*) FROM units) = 0 THEN

    SELECT 'Green Valley Apartments', 'greenvalley.society@okhdfcbank', 'Green Valley Apartments Owners Association', 'HDFC Bank', '50100234567890', 'HDFC0001234', 3, 5, 10
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM society_settings);

    ON CONFLICT (unit_number) DO NOTHING;

    ;

    ;

    ON CONFLICT (unit_id, period_month, period_year) DO NOTHING;

    ;

    ;

    ;

    ;

    ;

    ;

  END IF;
END $$;

